        "original_id": "8206589b-bcb7-59ec-aa83-556be5e5cde2",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Queens, Staten Island, Flushing Meadows–Corona Park\n- Products: Terrace on the Park\n- Systems: I-678 (Van Wyck Expressway), Grand Central Parkway\n- Places: Flushing Bay, LaGuardia Airport, Union Turnpike\n\nFacts:\n- Since 1899, the borough of Queens has been coterminous with Queens County.\n- In 2016, Queens had a census-estimated population of 2,333,054, making it the second-largest New York City borough by population after Brooklyn.\n- In 2016, approximately 48% of Queens residents were foreign-born.\n- In 2016, Staten Island had a census-estimated population of 476,015, making it the least populated New York City borough.\n- Staten Island is the third-largest New York City borough by area at 58 square miles.\n- Flushing Meadows–Corona Park is located in Queens between I-678 (Van Wyck Expressway) and the Grand Central Parkway.\n- Flushing Meadows–Corona Park stretches from Flushing Bay at the southern edge of LaGuardia Airport to Union Turnpike.\n- Terrace on the Park is a banquet hall in Flushing Meadows–Corona Park.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
